WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.340
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
in honor of Doctor Who doing Robin Hood I

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.560
wanted to do a video for my top 10 favorite
Fictional and Historical Characters inside

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.560
the canon.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.470
I just limited myself to Fantasy and Science
Fiction literature characters the doctor has

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.310
previously met or actual characters on screen.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.730
I also included real life historical people
they’ve parodied.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.400
Quick Reminder on the weekly giveaway, this
round is still open.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.109
All you have to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment.

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:28.359
On this video or my episode 3 review.

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:29.620
The comments are what I just randomly select
people from.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.400
There aren’t any spoilers for Episode 3
here so don’t worry if you haven’t watched

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.400
the episode yet.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.489
But starting with Number 10 - Stevie Wonder
in Good Man Goes To War Series 6 Episode 7.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:42.720
The Doctor snatched Stevie Wonder to play
for River’s birthday and took them both

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.720
back to 1814.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.860
It’s implied that it was Matt Smith’s
Doctor but it’s hard to tell since River

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.110
talks about meeting several of his different
incarnations.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:54.440
Like the time the doctor overlapped with his
own time line so that two of him were at one

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.440
of River’s birthday’s.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.360
I’m sure The Doctor Paid Stevie a very generous
fee.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.050
I also wonder how old Stevie was when the
doctor picked him up.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.500
Like did classic stevie wonder play for river
or current stevie wonder?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.650
Number 9 - Sigmund Freud in Curse of the Black
Spot from Series 6 Episode

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.420
This was just a name drop, Freud was one of
those real life historical figures that showed

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.750
up in a lot of the expanded material but he
get name dropped in the Doctor Who movie.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.680
Both time were references of the Doctor having
sat on Freud’s infamous couch.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.570
Given the psycho sexual nature of Freud’s
work we can only imagine what their conversations

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.570
must have been like.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:31.030
I feel like a good anniversary box set extra
would be a data file on freud’s analysis

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.630
of the Doctor.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.200
If any of you are real life psychology students
maybe you can confirm this, I heard that in

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.200
real life the actual Sigmund Freud felt like
people ended up twisting his ideas so that

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:48.300
most of what we think about psychoanalysis
is wrong.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.190
Number 8 - William Shakespeare In Shakespeare
Code from Series 3 episode 2

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.880
Another recurring historical character in
the canon.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.030
He’s been a part of at least 4 tv stories
not including shakespeare code.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.130
But the David Tennant one made him central
to the plot.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.840
It’s a very magic based story

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.740
I love how they have fun with the legend of
shakespeare versus the reality.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.800
Or the reality inside the doctor who universe.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.950
“Shut your big fat mouths” just sounds
so much better coming from the mouth of the

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:16.950
bard.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.080
The episode was written by Gareth Roberts
who wrote episode 6 of the current series.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.140
The Caretaker.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.450
He’s written a bunch of doctor who episodes.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.070
Number 7 - Houdini from Planet of the Ood
series 4 episode 3

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.670
I love Donna and the Tenth Doctor.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.810
Such a great buddy cop flick when those two
are together.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.060
Houdini was really used as a joke in this
story.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.280
Several different doctors mentioned meeting
and learning escape tricks from him.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.400
Planet of the Ood was funny because it was
a big joke on how the Doctor either couldn’t

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.470
competely figure out Houdini’s handcuffs
trick or that the trick was useless in the

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.490
future.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:54.240
Donna is one of the few people I can stand
ripping on the Doctor, she does it so well

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.599
it just feels right.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:57.849
Clara has made fun of Capaldi’s doctor a
little so far.

00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:59.950
But it’s a very different vibe than 10 and
Donna.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.680
Number 6 - Leonardo Davinci

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.950
He’s been featured in the comics but on
the show he’s mostly been referenced in

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:06.950
some way by various Doctors.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.220
The Sixth Doctor had a business card that
read davinci in the two doctors and the fourth

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.819
doctor talked about meeting him during City
of Death.

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:17.810
When I asked you guys for some of your favorites
the davinci speech from City of Death was

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.810
a common pick.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:25.110
The other funny thing is that Tom Riley actually
plays Leonardo Davinci on Davinci’s Demons.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:28.260
I’m not current with the show right now.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.890
But it’s a cool coincidence that bumped
him higher up my list.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.540
Crossover interactions like this are a lot
more common in British Television just because

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.240
projects tend to run for shorter periods of
time so actors have more free time and it’s

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.240
just more a part of the acting culture in
general for actors to float around.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.500
In the united states for example, especially
for bigger shows that run 20 or more episodes.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.940
Actors are book for most of the year so they
just don’t have as much time to guest star

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.940
on other shows.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.500
Number 5 - Winston Churchill in so many things

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.800
Ian McNiece is one of my favorite character
actors, usually when he’s playing villains.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.340
But it’s hard to forget his winston churchill.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.610
He’s another real life historical figure
that’s so famous, he just ends up being

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.940
parodied a lot.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.269
Not that I think Doctor Who’s version of
him was poking fun too much.

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:04.530
I think the series 6 finale is probably my
favorite appearance in recent memory.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.069
The episode is just so crazy that you kind
of forget about him at a certain point.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:11.980
But the idea that Churchill has become the
Holy Roman Emperor is so funny.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.170
It says a lot about what Moffat thinks of
his ego.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.909
To make himself an emperor.

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:23.150
We’re not meant to dig too deep, but you
start to wonder how he was able to depose

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.270
all the previous emperors.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.949
They way they treated the time paradox was
a little confusing.

00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:28.949
but whatever.

00:04:28.949 --> 00:04:32.339
Number 4 - Dracula in the Big Finish story
Son of the Dragon

00:04:32.339 --> 00:04:35.110
It’s a fifth doctor story about Vlad the
Impaler.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:40.020
The Doctor travels back to 1462 and it’s
more of a Vlad Dracula story than a traditional

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.349
vampire story.

00:04:41.349 --> 00:04:46.340
I’m a big fan of dracula stories that aren’t
straight up re-tellings of the Bram Stoker

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.340
tale.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:53.199
There’s even a new Dracula prequel of sorts
starring Luke Evans coming out October 10th.

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:56.580
In the Big Finish story the voice of dracula
is provided by James Purefoy from the Following.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.150
Number 3 - Queen Nefertiti in Dinosaurs on
a Spaceship

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:03.150
I love the ‘ship that develops between her
and Rupert Graves from Sherlock.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.819
So many fandoms in that episode.

00:05:04.819 --> 00:05:05.939
Including Harry Potter.

00:05:05.939 --> 00:05:10.650
One of the best moments she had was when she
met Amy and asked her if she was also a Queen.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:18.110
I feel like Amy let that go to her head thereafter
in a really adorable way.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:30.639
I’d say most if not all the female companions
are queen material.

00:05:30.639 --> 00:05:33.659
I feel like one of the reasons they chose
to use Nefertiti in the episode was because

00:05:33.659 --> 00:05:35.379
Cleopatra had already been done so much.

00:05:35.379 --> 00:05:38.410
There are only a handful of very notable ancient
queens.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.860
I would say Catherine the Great would be one
they haven’t used.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.199
I think the Cold War probably kept Classic
Who from using her character.

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:47.360
But let me know if there are any big queens
or powerful female figures from a long time

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.360
ago you want the show to do.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.439
Foxes the singer is going to be in Mummy on
the Orient Express this year.

00:05:53.439 --> 00:05:56.930
So we might see some more Cleopatra references.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.509
Number 2 - HItler from Let’s Kill Hitler

00:06:00.509 --> 00:06:05.490
This came after Inglorious Basterds did their
crazy version of Hitler and that came after

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.039
the Hitler Downfall movie.

00:06:07.039 --> 00:06:09.189
The one with that scene of Hitler going insane.

00:06:09.189 --> 00:06:11.030
In case you missed it, it was parodied to
infinity.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:14.349
Just search google or tumblr for Hitler goes
insane to find all the memes.

00:06:14.349 --> 00:06:18.240
This time they reduced the role to the point
of non speaking almost.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.240
It almost wasn’t even about Hitler.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.869
And I love that they make one of the most
infamous villains in modern history window

00:06:22.869 --> 00:06:25.180
dressing in a River Song story.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:30.310
Of course crazy Melody Pond would show up
in a hitler episode.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.249
Number 1 Vincent Van Gogh (other great artists
got shout outs)

00:06:33.249 --> 00:06:38.110
He’s my favorite mostly because the episode
in general is an emotional touchstone for

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:42.860
the Matt Smith era and for me personally but
because of the way it tied things back to

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.529
the Doctor’s future.

00:06:44.529 --> 00:06:52.620
Most of the episode is spent trying to analyze
the psychology of genius in a way that’s

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:53.620
relatable.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.789
Mostly genius doesn’t makes sense to all
of us because you’d have to be a genius

00:06:57.789 --> 00:06:59.270
to fully understand genius.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:04.129
But you have two mad men, one with a brush
and canvas and one with a blue box.

00:07:04.129 --> 00:07:06.419
Both will not be able to escape their destiny.

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:10.219
They couldn’t alter Van Gogh’s timeline
and all the terrible things from the Doctor’s

00:07:10.219 --> 00:07:14.439
future that we’ve learned about so far will
probably end up happening no matter what he

00:07:14.439 --> 00:07:15.439
does.

00:07:15.439 --> 00:07:17.979
I think solutions to changing the past like
the pocket universe in the 50th are just side

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:18.979
steps.

00:07:18.979 --> 00:07:19.979
Ultimately, left to their own devices.

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:21.960
The Time Lords will come back and the Time
War will restart.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.219
It’s going to be really interesting to see
how future doctor who series deal with that.

00:07:25.219 --> 00:07:30.919
Right now I think the only solution is for
the writers to keep Gallifrey in the pocket

00:07:30.919 --> 00:07:31.919
universe.

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:35.529
I do think Capaldi will find it eventually,
but I don’t think they’ll rush to bring

00:07:35.529 --> 00:07:37.219
it back into normal space.

00:07:37.219 --> 00:07:41.349
I think part of the reason they saved it in
the 50th from a production standpoint was

00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:45.139
so that someday they’d be able to do time
lord stories again.

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:50.050
But let me know who your favorite fictional
or historical character is from doctor who

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:54.449
and do you want to see the time lords come
back, like full on gallifrey come back, before

00:07:54.449 --> 00:07:55.889
Capaldi leaves the role.

00:07:55.889 --> 00:07:59.350
In case you didn’t see my earlier videos,
he’s signed on for series 9, it’s Jenna

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.240
Coleman that’s still undecided.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.000
Or at least unannounced.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.840
I’m still working on my Q&amp;A for tomorrow.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.029
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:07.029 --> 00:08:08.809
Still plenty of time to submit questions.

00:08:08.809 --> 00:08:13.119
I’ve been seeing a lot of good questions
about the promised land so far.

00:08:13.119 --> 00:08:16.789
Right now click here for that video, I’ll
update the annotation as soon as I post it

00:08:16.789 --> 00:08:18.581
and click here for my episode 3 review.

00:08:18.581 --> 00:08:21.990
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:24.799
High Fives!

